The Arris TR4400 v2 is a dual band router provided by Spectrum to customers as the "Wave 2" with model number RAC2V1A. It uses a Qualcomm IPQ8065 SoC with 512 MB RAM and 256 MB NAND flash.  There is also a SAC2V1A [[https://www.spectrum.net/en/support/internet/spectrum-wave-2-router-user-manual|device variant]] for the same FCCID and [[https://www.wi-fi.org/product-finder-results?keywords=WFA71730|WiFi Alliance certification]] (WFA71730) but with 1 GB RAM.

The device does not allow the user to flash firmware, does not support settings backup and restore, and does not provide access via SSH. The SSH server (dropbear) cannot start due to misconfiguration. And even if it could, the admin user shell has been replaced with a limited router configuration tool.  Serial port access is the only known way to root the device, but can be a painful process (see [[#hardware]] for details). Once the hardware issues are sorted out, the device is not protected: the bootloader can be interrupted, and also once the router has booted up, pressing enter drops you to a root shell. RAC2V1A [[https://github.com/Lanchon/tr4400-v2-stock-firmware/tree/master/r1418-2018-03-01|stock firmware]] uses OpenWrt Barrier Breaker r1121 build (other reported builds: 1418, 1602, 1782, 1806).  The default radio SSID's are //MySpectrumWifi{last 2 MAC characters}-2G// and //-5G//.

The SAC2V1A is based on Chaos Calmer 15.05.1 (r35193) and the back label references a QR code to use the Spectrum app for setup. The default radio SSID nomenclature changes to //SpectrumSetup-{last 2 MAC characters}// and OpenWrt installation is the same for the hardware and SSH access, but requires different [[#notes|steps]] using the [[#serial]] port.
